            <ArticleTitle>Age as a risk factor: you are as old as your arteries.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1455-7, A7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Advancing age is a major risk factor for coronary heart disease and is an indicator of coronary plaque burden. Noninvasive assessment of subclinical atherosclerosis is a better measurement of plaque burden and can provide a better assessment of &quot;arterial age.&quot;</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
